<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_Warcasket_Cataphract (VFEP v3.09, commit 31cee5e,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml); fields not discussed here are the Cataphract's,
    VFEP_AdvancedWarcaskets research prereq, WarcasketHeavy/WarcasketCata raid tags and the
    industrial steel/uranium costList included.

    Tuning. Reference numbers are VFEP's 5th-generation Cataphract, the heaviest pre-spacer set
    (Sharp 1.56 / Blunt 0.65 / Heat 0.78, Mass 75, MoveSpeed -0.85). The Toxin is that chassis
    resealed for chemical warfare, so plating, weight, speed and price stay the Cataphract's and
    the identity is carried by protection against toxins:
    - ToxicResistance +0.5 here and +0.5 on the helmet, VFEP's own 10th-generation split (its
      spacer armors and helmets each carry 0.5; shoulders never do). The full set reaches the
      stat's cap of 1.0, a chemical-warfare suit's whole point; VFEP's Hazard set gets there on
      its helmet alone (+1), so the cap has a precedent below spacer tier. ToxicResistance
      multiplies into every toxic buildup source, tox gas included
      (ToxicUtility.DoPawnToxicDamage), so at 1.0 the wearer takes no buildup from gas at all.
      Both stats are Core, so nothing here needs Biotech.
    - The emitter half of the identity (a tox gas ability) is deferred and will live behind the
      Biotech load-folder gate drafted in LoadFolders.xml; see TODOs.md. Costs may move when it
      lands, since a reagent tank would price onto this piece.

    Art: the texPaths point at VFEP's Cataphract textures as PLACEHOLDERS until the set's own
    art lands under Textures/Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketToxin/ (see TODOs.md). Texture
    lookup is global by path, so VFEP's art resolves from its own folder.

    Compat: 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml reaches this def (EVA tag, cold insulation).

    ApparelExtension priority 1: VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase carries its own ApparelExtension and
    inheritance appends list items, so this def resolves with two. VEF merges duplicate
    extensions in a Def.ResolveReferences prefix, highest priority surviving; at priority 1 every
    field of ours, from any load root, is kept. The Cataphract itself relies on the equal-priority
    merge, which happens to keep these same fields, but the guard costs nothing and any future
    field (a gated root's, say) needs it.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase">
    <defName>TXWC_Warcasket_Toxin</defName>
    <label>toxin warcasket</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized warcasket shell with superior protection and worse weight, sealed against chemical and toxic exposure.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized warcasket shell with superior protection and worse weight, sealed against chemical and toxic exposure.\n\n5th generation warcaskets were created with a much shorter period between generations, largely being slight specializations of the previous one. The Toxin design reworked the Cataphract chassis for chemical warfare: every seam gasketed, every intake filtered, so that a pilot could hold a gassed position long after everyone else had fled it.\n\nPirate crews took to seeding a raid with toxin pilots and shelling their own front line with gas. Whoever was still standing when the cloud thinned was wearing one. Their motto, muffled through the respirator, was to breathe easy.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketCataphract/WarcasketCataphract</texPath>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>75</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>1.56</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.65</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>0.78</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>43</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>14</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <MoveSpeed>-0.85</MoveSpeed>
      <ToxicResistance>0.5</ToxicResistance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.3</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentIndustrial>5</ComponentIndustrial>
      <Steel>175</Steel>
      <Uranium>50</Uranium>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_AdvancedWarcaskets</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Torso</li>
        <li>Legs</li>
        <li>Feet</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketCataphract/WarcasketCataphract</wornGraphicPath>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <li>WarcasketHeavy</li>
        <li>WarcasketCata</li>
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
        <traitsOnEquip>
          <li>VFEP_WarcasketTrait</li>
        </traitsOnEquip>
        <traitsOnUnequip>
          <li>VFEP_Shellcasket</li>
        </traitsOnUnequip>
        <pawnCapacityMinLevels>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
        </pawnCapacityMinLevels>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
